{"subjectId":"data-science","id":"scraping-projects","title":"Scraping Multiple Pages","group":"Web Scraping","order":8,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Real datasets span many pages. Loop over page URLs, reuse the same extraction code, collect rows, and save them as a table — the notebook's quotes and books scrapers.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-link\"></i>Page URLs</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>urls = [f\"https://quotes.toscrape.com/page/{page}/\" for page in range(1, 6)]\nprint(urls[0])       # https://quotes.toscrape.com/page/1/\nprint(len(urls))     # 5</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-table\"></i>Extract → rows → DataFrame</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>html = \"\"\"\n&lt;div class=\"quote\"&gt;\n  &lt;span class=\"text\"&gt;“The world as we have created it is a process of our thinking.”&lt;/span&gt;\n  &lt;small class=\"author\"&gt;Albert Einstein&lt;/small&gt; &lt;a href=\"/author/Albert-Einstein\"&gt;(about)&lt;/a&gt;\n  &lt;a class=\"tag\" href=\"/tag/change/\"&gt;change&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a class=\"tag\" href=\"/tag/thinking/\"&gt;thinking&lt;/a&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=\"quote\"&gt;\n  &lt;span class=\"text\"&gt;“It is our choices that show what we truly are.”&lt;/span&gt;\n  &lt;small class=\"author\"&gt;J.K. Rowling&lt;/small&gt; &lt;a href=\"/author/J-K-Rowling\"&gt;(about)&lt;/a&gt;\n  &lt;a class=\"tag\" href=\"/tag/choices/\"&gt;choices&lt;/a&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\"\"\"\n\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom bs4 import BeautifulSoup\n\ndef parse_quotes(html):\n    rows = []\n    for q in BeautifulSoup(html, \"html.parser\").find_all(\"div\", class_=\"quote\"):\n        rows.append({\n            \"quote\": q.find(\"span\", class_=\"text\").text[1:-1],       # strip the curly quotes\n            \"author\": q.find(\"small\", class_=\"author\").text,\n            \"details\": q.find(\"a\").get(\"href\"),\n            \"tags\": \",\".join(t.text for t in q.find_all(\"a\", class_=\"tag\")),\n        })\n    return rows\n\npages = [html, html]                        # stand-ins for page 1 and page 2\nrows = [row for page in pages for row in parse_quotes(page)]\ndf = pd.DataFrame(rows)\nprint(df.shape, df.columns.tolist())        # (4, 4) ['quote', 'author', 'details', 'tags']\nprint(df.loc[0, \"tags\"])                    # change,thinking\ndf.to_csv(\"quotes.csv\", index=False)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-world\"></i>The full live scraper</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import time\nimport requests\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom tqdm import tqdm                              # progress bar: pip install tqdm\n\nrows = []\nfor page in tqdm(range(1, 11)):\n    r = requests.get(f\"https://quotes.toscrape.com/page/{page}/\", timeout=10)\n    if r.status_code != 200:\n        break                                     # no more pages\n    rows += parse_quotes(r.text)\n    time.sleep(0.5)                               # be polite\npd.DataFrame(rows).to_csv(\"quotes.csv\", index=False)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-books\"></i>Books: fields from attributes</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>from bs4 import BeautifulSoup\nhtml = \"\"\"\n&lt;li class=\"col-xs-6 col-sm-4 col-md-3 col-lg-3\"&gt;&lt;article class=\"product_pod\"&gt;\n  &lt;a href=\"a-light-in-the-attic_1000/index.html\"&gt;&lt;img src=\"../media/cache/2c/da/cover.jpg\"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\n  &lt;p class=\"star-rating Three\"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;h3&gt;&lt;a href=\"a-light-in-the-attic_1000/index.html\" title=\"A Light in the Attic\"&gt;A Light in the ...&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;\n  &lt;p class=\"price_color\"&gt;£51.77&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p class=\"instock availability\"&gt; In stock &lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/article&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n\"\"\"\nbook = BeautifulSoup(html, \"html.parser\").find(\"article\", class_=\"product_pod\")\ntitle = book.h3.a[\"title\"]                                   # the full title lives in an attribute\nrating = book.find(\"p\", class_=\"star-rating\")[\"class\"][-1]   # the rating is a CSS class\nprice = float(book.find(\"p\", class_=\"price_color\").text.lstrip(\"£\"))\nstock = book.find(\"p\", class_=\"instock\").text.strip()\nlink = \"https://books.toscrape.com/catalogue/\" + book.h3.a[\"href\"]\nprint(title, rating, price, stock)     # A Light in the Attic Three 51.77 In stock\nprint(link)                            # https://books.toscrape.com/catalogue/a-light-in-the-attic_1000/index.html</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>Visible text is often shortened (“A Light in the ...”); the complete value sits in an attribute (<code>title</code>, <code>alt</code>, <code>data-*</code>). Inspect the page (right-click → <em>Inspect</em>) before writing selectors.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-join\"></i>Joining list pages with detail pages</h3>\n<p>The notebook scrapes 50 list pages for title/price/link, then visits each book's own page for extra fields (UPC, tax, reviews) and joins the two tables. Join on a shared key, not on row position:</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import pandas as pd\nbooks = pd.DataFrame({\"link\": [\"b1\", \"b2\"], \"title\": [\"Attic\", \"Velvet\"]})\ndetails = pd.DataFrame({\"link\": [\"b2\", \"b1\"], \"upc\": [\"u-2\", \"u-1\"]})\nprint(books.merge(details, on=\"link\").to_dict(\"records\"))\n# [{'link': 'b1', 'title': 'Attic', 'upc': 'u-1'}, {'link': 'b2', 'title': 'Velvet', 'upc': 'u-2'}]</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Correction</div><p>The notebook builds the final table with <code>df['UPC'] = df_2['UPC']</code> next to <code>df_1['Title']</code> — that only lines up if both lists are in exactly the same order and length. A failed detail page (the notebook's 404) silently shifts every row. Use <code>merge</code> on the link.</p></div></section>"}